cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this benchmark, please cite it as below."
title: KR-Housing-LongRAG-Bench
abstract: >-
  A copyright-safe Korean long-context benchmark for evaluating whether
  full-context LLMs can replace or complement RAG and table/tool pipelines over
  real housing announcements (입주자모집공고), public tabular data (MOLIT 실거래 /
  HUG 분양이력), and housing statutes. The public release contains QA labels,
  evidence locators, deterministic predicates, answerability labels, split and
  provider/region metadata, and long-context-bundle references — no raw source
  documents, no leaked answers, and no API keys. v0.9.2 keeps the 1,997 QA and
  splits of v0.9 (dev 1,608 / test_public 389) and their questions unchanged.
  Three annotators reviewed all 347 evaluated test_public items; 29 have an
  error (8.4%, Wilson 95% [5.9, 11.7]). This corrects the 0.8% one-author
  sample figure published with v0.9.1: the same 118 items have 8 errors under
  the three-annotator review. 24 gold answers are corrected in
  data/v0.9.2/gold_fixes.json and 5 ill-posed items are excluded from
  evaluation, leaving 342 evaluated test_public items; the legal family stays
  excluded as in v0.9.1. Dev was not reviewed by people; 54 dev items carry
  unverified automatic flags and are still evaluated. Errata are in
  data/errata_v0.9.2.csv. The primary judge is claude-sonnet-5-5 (98.8% agreement
  with 80 human labels) and gpt-4.1-mini is the secondary judge. The release is
  not leaderboard-ready and has no sealed hidden split.
type: dataset
version: v0.9.2
date-released: 2026-10-11
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/comsa33/kr-housing-longrag-bench"
